marbor - CLI client for the Marbor Admin API

Usage:
  marbor <command> [flags]

Commands:
  version    print CLI and (if reachable) server version
  status     print marbor health/status summary
  login      authenticate once and save the session locally (recommended)
  logout     remove the saved session
  whoami     show the CLI's saved identity (live-verified)
  nodes      list nodes known to marbor
  models     fleet-wide list, or pull/delete/unload/list on one node
  runtime    start/stop/restart/logs/drain/undrain/health on one node
  node       node control driver operations
  key        per-API-key local/cloud routing overrides (masked list, plaintext-once on create)
  schedules  manage time-of-day warmup/unload/drain/undrain automations (P-A2-03)
  routing    manage routing rules and global routing strategy (P-A2-04)
  spill      show per-key, per-provider local-vs-cloud request counts
  activity   show unified fleet activity feed (drain, agent, runtime, node, warmup, schedule, predictive, config)
  requests   inspect routing decisions for past requests
  audit      inspect the persisted, filterable request audit log (P-A2-08a)
  users      manage dashboard users

Run "marbor <command> --help" for the full list of actions and flags for
that command.

Global flags:
  --server string    Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MARBOR_SERVER)
  --json             output machine-readable JSON instead of a human table
  --username string  admin username, used to log in (env MARBOR_USERNAME)
  --password string  admin password, used to log in (env MARBOR_PASSWORD)

"nodes", "models", "runtime", and "node control" require credentials: run
"marbor login" once (recommended), or pass --username+--password (or
MARBOR_USERNAME+MARBOR_PASSWORD) on every invocation instead.
"version" and "status" do not require credentials.
